==Strategy==
For the final stage of probably the hardest of the three Behemoth Culling Maps, and likely the last Behemoth Culling stage you'll ever beat, this stage is surprisingly not extremely difficult. A horde of dangerous Aliens paired with a strong Floating backliner that nukes all your units if you push too hard makes this stage reminiscent of [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 1's [[The Big Bang (Cats of the Cosmos)|Big Bang]]. Simply bring powerful anti-Aliens such as [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], as well as high speed rushers such as [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and Courier Cat, and the stage is all but yours. Simply stall at the beginning for money, and don't push too hard lest your units are annihilated by Ensanglion's extreme damage.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] - A solid emergency meatshield as it can halt the enemies' movement after each Ensanglion's attack.
*[[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] - An amazing Tanker against Alien Behemoths, especially when they're weakened and if they're a high level (Lv.40+).
*[[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]] - Can tank a hit from Ensanglion at Lv.38+ and has decent health to be useful against the other enemies, especially the Behemoths.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] - One of the few Cats that can't be one-shot by Ensanglion, or the other enemies with high damage, like Wild Doge.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - A staple in any Behemoth stage, since they have a quick recharge and high damage.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Fishman as an Anti-Floating can take a bunch of health off of Ensanglion. Specifically 1/28 of Ensanglion's Health at Level 50.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]] - Massive damage against Aliens with a large LD range, can easily clear the alien peons present in the stage. She also outranges Ensanglion's Omni Strike, but caution needs to be taken, as she'll die if the boss pushes any closer to her.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] - His standing range is able to outrange Ensanglion's Omni Strike, and has massive damage against all traits, he can be very helpful here. However, he does not outrange Crustaceous Scissorex's LD, so be careful when using him.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] - He does exceptionally well, since he outranges every enemy here. If you're lucky enough to have him and his Ultra Form, he's an obvious pick that vaporizes this stage with his absurd damage output and Knockback VS. Floating. Beware, if you don't protected him properly, Cosmo can easily die, so [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] and [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] synergize excellently with Supernova Cosmo.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lone Moon Lunos]] - At lv 50, he wields 145,800 HP (583,200 VS. All Traitless Enemies here & 729,000 VS. The Aliens & Ensanglion who is a Floating) which, combined with the fact that he is Tough against every single enemy in this stage, makes him pretty much a braindead carry here. Simply meatshield normally and time his conjure. You either want his conjure to kill the peons or make both the conjure and the wave attack hit the main threats.

